a3cac381 (255 1790639012563 "guenchi" () (set "8pniyrtk.1x" src ":root{--bg:#fbfaf7;--bg2:#f3f1ea;--panel:#f7f5ef;--line:#e4e0d5;--fg:#1c1b18;\n  --dim:#6a655c;--acc:#12b09c;--acc2:#0d8a7a;--gold:#9a6b12;--teal:#0f6f68;\n  --kw:#1a8f8f;--str:#0f6f3f;--com:#8a857a;--num:#8a4b12}\n*{margin:0;padding:0;box-sizing:border-box}\nhtml{scroll-behavior:smooth}\nbody{background:var(--bg);color:var(--fg);\n  font:16px/1.65 -apple-system,BlinkMacSystemFont,\\\"Segoe UI\\\",Roboto,\\\"Helvetica Neue\\\",Arial,sans-serif;\n  -webkit-font-smoothing:antialiased}\ncode,pre,.mono{font-family:ui-monospace,\\\"SF Mono\\\",SFMono-Regular,Menlo,Consolas,\\\"Liberation Mono\\\",monospace}\na{color:var(--acc2);text-decoration:none}\na:hover{text-decoration:underline}\n.wrap{max-width:1040px;margin:0 auto;padding:0 24px}\n.narrow{max-width:760px}\nnav{position:sticky;top:0;z-index:10;background:rgba(251,250,247,.88);\n  backdrop-filter:blur(8px);border-bottom:1px solid var(--line)}\nnav .wrap{display:flex;align-items:center;height:56px;gap:22px}\nnav .logo{font-weight:700;color:var(--fg);font-size:17px;letter-spacing:-.2px}\nnav .logo span{color:var(--acc);font-size:20px;vertical-align:-1px}\nnav .links{margin-left:auto;display:flex;gap:18px;font-size:14px}\nnav .links a{color:var(--dim)}\nnav .links a:hover{color:var(--fg);text-decoration:none}\nnav .links a.on{color:var(--fg);font-weight:600}\nheader{padding:80px 0 56px;position:relative;overflow:hidden;\n  background:radial-gradient(60% 50% at 50% 0%,#e4f4f4 0%,transparent 100%)}\nheader .wrap{position:relative;z-index:1}\n.glyph{font-size:44px;color:var(--acc);line-height:1}\nh1{font-size:54px;letter-spacing:-1.2px;margin:10px 0 16px}\n.tag{font-size:21px;color:var(--dim);max-width:660px;margin-bottom:12px}\n.tag b{color:var(--fg);font-weight:600}\n.sub{color:var(--dim);font-size:15px;margin-bottom:30px}\n.cta{display:flex;gap:14px;margin-bottom:38px;flex-wrap:wrap}\n.btn{display:inline-block;padding:11px 22px;border-radius:8px;font-size:15px;font-weight:600}\n.btn.primary{background:var(--acc);color:#fff}\n.btn.primary:hover{filter:brightness(1.12);text-decoration:none}\n.btn.ghost{border:1px solid var(--line);color:var(--fg)}\n.btn.ghost:hover{border-color:var(--dim);text-decoration:none}\nsection{padding:64px 0;border-top:1px solid var(--line)}\n.kicker{color:var(--acc);font-size:12px;font-weight:700;letter-spacing:2px;text-transform:uppercase}\nh2{font-size:32px;margin:8px 0 14px;letter-spacing:-.5px}\nh3{font-size:21px;margin-bottom:10px}\np{margin-bottom:14px}\n.lead{color:var(--dim);font-size:17px;max-width:700px}\n.grid2{display:grid;grid-template-columns:1fr 1fr;gap:36px;margin-top:36px}\n.grid2>*{min-width:0}\n.card{background:var(--panel);border:1px solid var(--line);border-radius:12px;padding:22px 24px}\n.card h3{font-size:18px;margin-bottom:8px}\n.card p{color:var(--dim);font-size:15px;margin-bottom:0}\n.card p+p{margin-top:10px}\n.nums{display:grid;grid-template-columns:repeat(auto-fit,minmax(170px,1fr));gap:1px;\n  background:var(--line);border:1px solid var(--line);border-radius:12px;overflow:hidden;margin-top:32px}\n.num{background:var(--bg);padding:20px}\n.num b{display:block;font-size:30px;letter-spacing:-.5px;color:var(--acc);margin-bottom:6px}\n.num span{color:var(--dim);font-size:13.5px;line-height:1.5;display:block}\npre{background:var(--bg2);border:1px solid var(--line);border-radius:10px;padding:18px 20px;\n  overflow-x:auto;font-size:13px;line-height:1.6}\npre.wide{font-size:12.5px}\ncode{color:var(--acc);font-size:.86em;background:var(--bg2);padding:1px 5px;border-radius:4px}\npre code{background:none;padding:0;color:inherit;font-size:inherit}\n.k{color:var(--kw)}.s{color:var(--str)}.c{color:var(--com);font-style:italic}.n{color:var(--num)}\ntable{border-collapse:collapse;width:100%;margin-top:24px;font-size:14.5px}\nth,td{border:1px solid var(--line);padding:9px 12px;text-align:left;vertical-align:top}\nth{background:var(--bg2);font-weight:600}\ntd.mono,th.mono{font-family:ui-monospace,Menlo,monospace;font-size:13px;white-space:nowrap}\n.verb{border-top:1px solid var(--line);padding:16px 0}\n.verb:first-child{border-top:none}\n.verb .sig{font-family:ui-monospace,Menlo,monospace;font-size:13.5px;color:var(--fg);\n  background:var(--bg2);border:1px solid var(--line);border-radius:6px;padding:7px 10px;\n  display:block;overflow-x:auto;white-space:pre}\n.verb .d{color:var(--dim);font-size:15px;margin-top:8px}\n.verb .r{float:right;font-size:11px;letter-spacing:1px;text-transform:uppercase;\n  color:var(--dim);border:1px solid var(--line);border-radius:4px;padding:1px 6px;margin-left:8px}\n.note{border-left:3px solid var(--gold);background:#fdfaf2;padding:14px 18px;\n  border-radius:0 8px 8px 0;margin-top:24px;font-size:15px;color:var(--dim)}\n.note b{color:var(--fg)}\n.steps{counter-reset:s;margin-top:28px}\n.step{position:relative;padding-left:46px;margin-bottom:26px}\n.step:before{counter-increment:s;content:counter(s);position:absolute;left:0;top:-2px;\n  width:30px;height:30px;border-radius:50%;background:var(--acc);color:#fff;\n  font-size:14px;font-weight:700;display:flex;align-items:center;justify-content:center}\n.step h3{font-size:18px;margin-bottom:6px}\n.step p{color:var(--dim);font-size:15px;margin-bottom:0}\nfooter{border-top:1px solid var(--line);padding:40px 0;color:var(--dim);font-size:14px}\nfooter .wrap{display:flex;gap:18px;flex-wrap:wrap;align-items:center}\nfooter .sp{margin-left:auto}\n.diagram{margin-top:36px}\n.diagram svg{width:100%;height:auto;display:block}\n@media (max-width:760px){\n  h1{font-size:38px}\n  header{padding:56px 0 40px}\n  .tag{font-size:18px}\n  .grid2{grid-template-columns:1fr;gap:24px}\n  nav .wrap{gap:12px}\n  nav .links{gap:11px;font-size:12.5px}\n  section{padding:48px 0}\n  h2{font-size:26px}\n}\n.subsec{margin-top:38px}\n.subsec h3{font-size:20px;margin-bottom:10px}\n.subsec h4{font-size:16px;margin:24px 0 8px}\n.subsec p{color:var(--dim)}\n.subsec .lead{color:var(--dim)}\nol.design{margin:18px 0 0 22px;color:var(--dim)}\nol.design li{margin:10px 0}\nol.design li b{color:var(--fg);font-weight:600}\nul.design{margin:18px 0 0 22px;color:var(--dim);list-style:none;padding:0}\nul.design li{margin:14px 0;padding-left:18px;border-left:3px solid var(--acc)}\nul.design li b{color:var(--fg);font-weight:600}\n.md-body{max-width:820px;margin:0 auto;padding:56px 24px}\n.md-body h1{font-size:40px;letter-spacing:-1px;margin-bottom:8px}\n.md-body h2{font-size:28px;margin:44px 0 12px;padding-top:22px;border-top:1px solid var(--line)}\n.md-body h3{font-size:20px;margin:30px 0 8px}\n.md-body h4{font-size:16px;margin:22px 0 6px;color:var(--fg)}\n.md-body p{color:var(--dim);margin:0 0 14px}\n.md-body blockquote{margin:18px 0;padding:12px 18px;border-left:3px solid var(--gold);background:#fdfaf2;border-radius:0 8px 8px 0}\n.md-body blockquote p{margin:0}\n.md-body pre{margin:14px 0}\n.md-body code{color:var(--acc)}"))
4e1e8db8 (256 1790687795720 "guenchi" () (set "8pniyrtk.31" body (define (favicon) "<svg xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\" viewBox=\"0 0 64 64\"><g transform=\"translate(32 32) scale(0.931) translate(-2.79 -1.11) rotate(21.77) translate(-32 -32)\"><g transform=\"translate(32 32) skewX(-12) translate(-32 -32)\" fill=\"none\" stroke-linecap=\"butt\"><path d=\"M35.0 10.0 V54.0 M48.750 4.0 V48.0 M35.0 29.0 H48.750\" stroke=\"#12b09c\" stroke-width=\"6.5\"/><path d=\"M10.75 22.75 H31.75\" stroke=\"#12b09c\" stroke-width=\"6.5\"/><path d=\"M21.25 22.75 V60.0\" stroke=\"#12b09c\" stroke-width=\"6.5\"/></g></g></svg>")))
ec5354cf (257 1790689746227 "guenchi" () (put ((kind . section) (title . "Installing") (src . "Section: Installing") (keywords . "install, prerequisites, homebrew, npm, compile, source") (parent . root) (ord . 11))))
2743f27c (258 1790689757517 "guenchi" () (move "8pniyrtk.75" root 7/2))
6ebfa340 (259 1790689829781 "guenchi" () (put ((kind . section) (title . "Silent write errors") (src . "Plain text offers zero structural validation on write. When an agent makes a bad edit or a botched patch, it fails silently — quietly dropping a design section or mangling code without throwing an error. And if the agent reads the file back after every write just to verify its own work, it doubles the token burn.") (keywords . "write, error, silent, validation, patch, verify") (parent . "8pniyrtk.k") (ord . 9))))
a8a1d8e8 (260 1790689863478 "guenchi" () (set "8pniyrtk.11" title "Concurrent overwrites and environment collisions"))
4d2ceb02 (261 1790689869353 "guenchi" () (set "8pniyrtk.11" src "Traditional files have no block-level isolation. When multiple agents and humans reason in parallel and edit the same docs or source files, they blindly overwrite each other's work — and if they try to build or test in a shared working directory, they corrupt each other's execution state."))
8880529e (262 1790689879184 "guenchi" () (set "8pniyrtk.y" title "The token black hole"))
319699fb (263 1790689879368 "guenchi" () (set "8pniyrtk.y" src "Beyond the cost of write-verification, everyday reading is equally wasteful. Docs and source files tend to grow monotonically — N lines added, zero deleted. Because the file is the unit of addressing, an agent that only needs one specific rule or function is forced to read the entire monolith, burning through its context window."))
84f4a91f (264 1790689888954 "guenchi" () (set "8pniyrtk.10" title "Runaway long-tail sprawl"))
557703ad (265 1790689889149 "guenchi" () (set "8pniyrtk.10" src "Over time, a file-based knowledge base inevitably decays into two extremes: thousands of isolated, atomic notes, and a handful of massive files accumulated over months. Splitting those monoliths by hand only shatters the logical flow."))
c536b6c7 (266 1790689897986 "guenchi" () (set "8pniyrtk.12" title "Drifting indexes"))
60f07eae (267 1790689898166 "guenchi" () (set "8pniyrtk.12" src "External vector indexes and line-number mappings are detached from the text itself. The moment a paragraph or function moves, the index goes stale without warning — feeding hallucinations to the agent while leaving cross-file semantic breaks invisible to Git."))
27023b30 (268 1790690077551 "guenchi" () (move "8pniyrtk.77" "8pniyrtk.k" 10))
7eaf9d5f (269 1790690176783 ("guenchi" ("8pniyrtk" . "w-34061-1790690176723-1") plan "a3ab01660306a7232288308213f41495dab2e39181720beff50ab6a880283a34" #f ("8pniyrtk" . 268)) () (plan "w-34061-1790690176723-1" "a3ab01660306a7232288308213f41495dab2e39181720beff50ab6a880283a34" ("8pniyrtk" . 268) ((0 set "8pniyrtk.2i" src "(define (page-why)\n  (shell \"Why not markdown | Theourgia\"\n    \"Five systemic walls that file-per-note memory hits as the substrate for multi-agent systems.\"\n    \"Why\"\n    (list\n      (phead \"Why not markdown\"\n        \"Markdown and plain source files are great for humans to write in, but as the underlying memory and engineering substrate for multi-agent systems, physical files hit five systemic walls.\")\n      (sec \"write\" \"01\" \"Silent write errors\"\n        (copy \"Silent write errors\"))\n      (sec \"concurrency\" \"02\" \"Concurrent overwrites and environment collisions\"\n        (copy \"Concurrent overwrites and environment collisions\")\n        (quasiquote (p (@ (style \"margin-top:20px\"))\n          (a (@ (href \"index.html#concurrency\"))\n            \"Drafts, commits and what a refusal hands back\") \" ->\")))\n      (sec \"read\" \"03\" \"The token black hole\"\n        (copy \"The token black hole\")\n        (prose \"Reading is all or nothing, measured\")\n        (table-of \"Query cost table\")\n        (quasiquote (p (@ (class \"lead\") (style \"margin-top:18px\"))\n          \"Fifty-six questions over twenty documents. The share is of what reading the \"\n          \"whole document every time would have cost.\")))\n      (sec \"shape\" \"04\" \"Runaway long-tail sprawl\"\n        (copy \"Runaway long-tail sprawl\"))\n      (sec \"index\" \"05\" \"Drifting indexes\"\n        (copy \"Drifting indexes\")\n        (quasiquote (div (@ (class \"grid2\"))\n          (unquote (card \"What a rename actually does\"))\n          (unquote (card \"Editing one sentence\"))))\n        (table-of \"Edit cost table\")))))")) (consumes "ws-session" (("8pniyrtk.2i" "e1f888724d8dd1fc1ae905d9a79f05b7939e1c2ad034b328cce6842b66cb082e" "8d500a82f1e50c288940966a5f976bfd25e7ffd55ec9a9412489968df8bfe6a5" (("8pniyrtk" . 268)))))))
ada356bc (270 1790690176868 ("guenchi" ("8pniyrtk" . "w-34061-1790690176723-1") 0 "a3ab01660306a7232288308213f41495dab2e39181720beff50ab6a880283a34" ("8pniyrtk" . 269) ("8pniyrtk" . 268)) () (set "8pniyrtk.2i" src "(define (page-why)\n  (shell \"Why not markdown | Theourgia\"\n    \"Five systemic walls that file-per-note memory hits as the substrate for multi-agent systems.\"\n    \"Why\"\n    (list\n      (phead \"Why not markdown\"\n        \"Markdown and plain source files are great for humans to write in, but as the underlying memory and engineering substrate for multi-agent systems, physical files hit five systemic walls.\")\n      (sec \"write\" \"01\" \"Silent write errors\"\n        (copy \"Silent write errors\"))\n      (sec \"concurrency\" \"02\" \"Concurrent overwrites and environment collisions\"\n        (copy \"Concurrent overwrites and environment collisions\")\n        (quasiquote (p (@ (style \"margin-top:20px\"))\n          (a (@ (href \"index.html#concurrency\"))\n            \"Drafts, commits and what a refusal hands back\") \" ->\")))\n      (sec \"read\" \"03\" \"The token black hole\"\n        (copy \"The token black hole\")\n        (prose \"Reading is all or nothing, measured\")\n        (table-of \"Query cost table\")\n        (quasiquote (p (@ (class \"lead\") (style \"margin-top:18px\"))\n          \"Fifty-six questions over twenty documents. The share is of what reading the \"\n          \"whole document every time would have cost.\")))\n      (sec \"shape\" \"04\" \"Runaway long-tail sprawl\"\n        (copy \"Runaway long-tail sprawl\"))\n      (sec \"index\" \"05\" \"Drifting indexes\"\n        (copy \"Drifting indexes\")\n        (quasiquote (div (@ (class \"grid2\"))\n          (unquote (card \"What a rename actually does\"))\n          (unquote (card \"Editing one sentence\"))))\n        (table-of \"Edit cost table\")))))"))
64675a84 (271 1790690313858 "guenchi" () (del "8pniyrtk.2i"))
43b05209 (272 1790690331269 "guenchi" () (put ((kind . code) (mode . datum) (lang . chez) (body define (page-why) (shell "Why not markdown | Theourgia" "Five systemic walls that file-per-note memory hits as the substrate for multi-agent systems." "Why" (list (phead "Why not markdown" "Markdown and plain source files are great for humans to write in, but as the underlying memory and engineering substrate for multi-agent systems, physical files hit five systemic walls.") (sec "write" "01" "Silent write errors" (copy "Silent write errors")) (sec "concurrency" "02" "Concurrent overwrites and environment collisions" (copy "Concurrent overwrites and environment collisions") (quasiquote (p (@ (style "margin-top:20px")) (a (@ (href "index.html#concurrency")) "Drafts, commits and what a refusal hands back") " ->"))) (sec "read" "03" "The token black hole" (copy "The token black hole") (prose "Reading is all or nothing, measured") (table-of "Query cost table") (quasiquote (p (@ (class "lead") (style "margin-top:18px")) "Fifty-six questions over twenty documents. The share is of what reading the " "whole document every time would have cost."))) (sec "shape" "04" "Runaway long-tail sprawl" (copy "Runaway long-tail sprawl")) (sec "index" "05" "Drifting indexes" (copy "Drifting indexes") (quasiquote (div (@ (class "grid2")) (unquote (card "What a rename actually does")) (unquote (card "Editing one sentence")))) (table-of "Edit cost table"))))) (doc . "") (parent . "8pniyrtk.2") (ord . 68))))
5bafe7bc (273 1790690770279 "guenchi" () (set "8pniyrtk.4p" src "To get past these limits, the system stops organizing content by files. Blocks now store both documentation and actual source code files. The underlying store still projects onto standard files when needed, but a file boundary no longer decides what is read, what is written, or what is run. Instead, we rebuilt how engineering knowledge and code are structured, assembled, tested, and computed across seven core mechanisms."))
bb075f9a (274 1790690779293 "guenchi" () (set "8pniyrtk.4q" src "We built a compact interface strictly for machine economics and token budgets, stripping out rendering markup entirely. Core verbs like outline, search, refs, and batch answer in dense S-expressions, one item per line. An agent can see the exact token footprint of what it is about to read before reading it—and there is no second, pretty-printed output mode to parse."))
5ac834e0 (275 1790690789622 "guenchi" () (set "8pniyrtk.4s" src "The wall between the code repository and the document store is a filesystem accident, not a property of the work itself. Here, blocks hold both Markdown documentation and source code files—everything engineering produces lives in one unified graph. A design section, a full source file, a Scheme macro, a Python function, and an architectural decision record are all equal blocks, each with its own stable ID and each independently addressable. Edges are typed and directed: a requirement points to the code that meets it, the code points to the test that checks it, and the test points back to the discussion that decided it."))
0494096a (276 1790690797592 "guenchi" () (set "8pniyrtk.4t" src "The graph changes how an agent—or a human—hunts for context, and what that hunt costs. A single refs query answers the whole picture at once: which design mentions this function? which prose block refers to it? Meanwhile, log hands back the block's exact history, and search pinpoints the answering block so the agent reads only that block instead of the entire file around it."))
54ce9349 (277 1790690807842 "guenchi" () (set "8pniyrtk.4u" src "An agent's real bottleneck isn't I/O speed—it's whether the tens of thousands of bytes entering its context window are actually right and complete. Today, agents assemble context by intuition: run a search, read a few blocks, feel like it's enough, and start coding. If they miss a premise or follow a superseded ruling, the mistake only surfaces after the work is done. We turn \"gathering materials\" from an agent's heuristic into a deterministic store verb—and make the store accountable for its choices."))
322fb9f9 (278 1790690818364 "guenchi" () (set "8pniyrtk.4v" src "The store isn't just for the automated half; it is a shared semantic layer where humans and agents work on the exact same code blocks, prose blocks, edges, and history. For humans, that means an IDE, not a CLI. Because people edit real files projected by the store, the Language Server works natively with zero loss of IntelliSense—while the extension maps every save back to the blocks it touched and adds what only the graph knows:"))
5009a087 (279 1790690825976 "guenchi" () (set "8pniyrtk.4w" src "Multiple agents and humans can edit and test the exact same code or documentation block simultaneously without locking up the store or stepping on each other's runtime state."))
5ff64677 (280 1790690845367 "guenchi" () (set "8pniyrtk.5g" src "Above Every Definition, What Only the Graph Knows:|A semantic lens sits right above each function: three design sections refer to this, two lessons learned, last changed by agent-b under request R, see test W3. Hovering reveals the design summary. While the language server tells you what a symbol is, the graph tells you why it is here, who depends on it, and what to read before changing it.\nA Rename That Names the Docs It Left Behind:|An editor rename writes back as one atomic change. Because block IDs never move, every edge from a design section, lesson, or test survives intact. One query for the old name then lists the exact prose paragraphs that haven't caught up—flagging stale documentation by name instead of hoping somebody notices.\nAn Agent's Draft, Reviewed with the Whole IDE:|Each writer's scratchpad is its own indexed workspace root. You review an agent's unfinished code change alongside its design, references, and live diagnostics rather than squinting at a flat text diff—and the agent sees those exact same IDE diagnostics and test results on its draft before committing.\nPrecision Test Runs:|With call hierarchies stored as graph edges, knowing which tests must rerun is a single graph walk from the changed block: only the tests that guard it, and the tests that guard its callers, get executed."))
6c624070 (281 1790690860582 "guenchi" () (put ((kind . section) (title . "F7 lead") (src . "The store is not just where knowledge and code are kept; it is a runtime they execute in.") (keywords . "lisp, machine, runtime, evaluate, sandbox, history") (parent . "8pniyrtk.j") (ord . 21))))
50a3f65a (282 1790690869878 "guenchi" () (put ((kind . section) (title . "F3 measurement") (src . "Measured across 56 questions over 20 real engineering documents: searching and reading the target block costs 15% of the tokens required to read the full document each time; browsing the outline before reading costs 20%. The outline of an entire corpus takes up just 6% of its raw Markdown size.") (keywords . "backlinks, tokens, cost, measured, outline, search") (parent . "8pniyrtk.j") (ord . 22))))
3f91d98b (283 1790690887370 "guenchi" () (put ((kind . section) (title . "Context sub-features") (src . "In-Memory Datalog Queries (query):|The store's reduced in-memory state is treated as a set of logical facts: blocks, their types, validity, and versions; block fields; parent-child trees; library definitions; verification records; task premises; and typed edges (depends, uses, implements, supersedes, refutes). Over these facts sits a fixed set of Datalog-style rules built right into the core. Evaluation runs purely in memory—no disk writes, no log scanning, and no user code execution. Agents can directly ask for dependency chains, blast radiuses, unresolved rulings, expired verifications, or the single authoritative definition of a name in scope without walking the graph by hand.\nBudget-Bounded Context Compilation (context):|Given a task block (carrying its premises, goals, and deliverables) and a strict token budget, context selects and categorizes the exact working set: Constraints (Must-Read) include the task's premises and their dependency closure, unresolved rulings in the subtree, and the unique, live, authoritative definition for every symbol the task touches within its scope. Evidence, Counterexamples, Background, and Stale Verifications fill the remaining token budget greedily in a documented order. Explicit Exclusions list every block left out due to budget limits alongside the exact reason it missed the cut.") (keywords . "context, query, datalog, budget, compilation, deterministic") (parent . "8pniyrtk.j") (ord . 23))))
a3c03413 (284 1790690904563 "guenchi" () (put ((kind . section) (title . "Concurrency sub-features") (src . "Isolated Scratchpads:|Every human and agent operates under a writer id—from which block IDs are minted, so every block carries its author's identity for life. Calling write places a proposed code or prose change into the writer's private scratchpad, invisible to the log and to everyone else. The main tree stays untouched until someone commits.\nConcurrent Execution and Testing in Dedicated Environments:|A scratchpad is not a dead text buffer. Code modified concurrently inside a scratchpad runs and tests inside its own dedicated, isolated environment. Ten agents can explore ten competing implementations of the same module at the same time—compiling, executing, and running test suites in parallel within their own scratchpad environments—verifying that their changes actually work before ever touching the main tree.\nBaseline Optimistic Locking:|commit installs a writer's verified drafts into the store as one atomic change, serialized by the store process so races are cleanly decided rather than interleaved. When a commit declares the version it was based on and that baseline has moved, the store never silently overwrites. Instead, it refuses the commit with stale-baseline—handing back the version the draft was made against, the current version, and the records applied since (including the winner's content). The losing agent already holds everything it needs to merge the changes inside its scratchpad, rerun its tests, and commit again.") (keywords . "scratchpad, writer, isolation, concurrent, execution, locking") (parent . "8pniyrtk.j") (ord . 24))))
beeef23d (285 1790690916908 "guenchi" () (put ((kind . section) (title . "Lisp Machine sub-features") (src . "In-Block Sandboxed Evaluation:|When a block holds Scheme code, the system acts as a modern Lisp machine. Both agent-generated and human-typed code evaluate in place against the R6RS libraries and definitions held in the store. Every evaluation runs inside an isolated child process with strict wall-clock, memory, and output quotas, returning standard output cleanly in its own response field.\nEvaluate at Any Point in History:|Because the store's state is a deterministic reduction of the log, you can evaluate code at any historical cut. You aren't just diffing old source text—you are executing the old behavior as the system stood at that moment, with the exact historical coordinate returned so the run can always be reproduced.") (keywords . "lisp, sandbox, evaluation, history, R6RS, child process") (parent . "8pniyrtk.j") (ord . 25))))
c4a28f16 (286 1790690924933 "guenchi" () (put ((kind . section) (title . "Context two layers") (src . "It works in two layers:") (keywords . "context, layers, query, compilation") (parent . "8pniyrtk.j") (ord . 26))))
c70ffab1 (287 1790690934995 "guenchi" () (del "8pniyrtk.2b"))
777fdb57 (288 1790690973782 "guenchi" () (put ((kind . code) (mode . datum) (lang . chez) (body define (page-index) (shell "Theourgia -- a block-graph storage engine for LLM agents" "A knowledge base agents and people write into together: a minimal query surface, one graph across code and prose, backlinks in one query, deterministic context assembly, a shared editor, scratchpads with per-block optimistic commits, and Scheme blocks that run." "Home" (list (quasiquote (header (div (@ (class "wrap")) (div (@ (class "glyph")) (raw "&#952;")) (h1 "Theourgia") (p (@ (class "tag")) (unquote (copy "Tagline"))) (p (@ (class "sub")) (unquote (copy "Hero sub"))) (div (@ (class "cta")) (a (@ (class "btn primary") (href "https://github.com/guenchi/theourgia")) "Get the code") (a (@ (class "btn ghost") (href "why.html")) "Why not markdown") (a (@ (class "btn ghost") (href "manual.html")) "The 32 verbs"))))) (sec "features" "Core features" "A Living Graph Engine for Human-Agent Symbiosis" #f (prose "Core features lead")) (sec "query" "01" "A Minimal Query Surface for Agents" (copy "F1 lead") (code-of "F1 example")) (sec "graph" "02" "One Unified Graph Across Docs and Source Code" (copy "F2 lead") (graph-svg) (quasiquote (div (@ (class "grid2")) (unquote (card "A name is a block")) (unquote (card "Other languages, more modestly")))) (quasiquote (p (@ (style "margin-top:22px")) (a (@ (href "manual.html")) "The store, the block and the log, in full") " ->"))) (sec "refs" "03" "Global Backlinks at Near-Zero Cost" (copy "F3 lead") (code-of "Refs, verbatim") (prose "F3 measurement") (table-of "F3 cost table") (note-of "What refs resolves, exactly")) (sec "context" "04" "Deterministic Context Assembly" (copy "F4 lead") (prose "Context two layers") (ulist-of "Context sub-features")) (sec "people" "05" "Human-Agent Symbiosis in the IDE" (copy "F5 lead") (ulist-of "IDE scarce uses")) (sec "concurrency" "06" "Zero-Conflict Concurrent Workspaces & Isolated Execution" (copy "F6 lead") (ulist-of "Concurrency sub-features") (code-of "A refusal, verbatim") (note-of "About that example")) (sec "evaluate" "07" "A Lisp Machine: A Living Knowledge Base" (copy "F7 lead") (ulist-of "Lisp Machine sub-features") (code-of "History evaluation, verbatim") (quasiquote (p (@ (class "lead") (style "margin-top:18px")) "The definition was changed between the two calls. The second asks for the " "earlier cut and gets the behaviour that was there then."))) (sec "measured" "Measured" "Numbers, and where they came from" #f (nums-panel "Numbers") (note-of "How the numbers were taken")) (sec "start" "Start" "A store is a directory" #f (code-of "Quickstart") (quasiquote (p (@ (class "lead") (style "margin-top:22px")) (unquote (copy "Install")))))))) (doc . "") (parent . "8pniyrtk.2") (ord . 69))))
41b05209 (289 1790691087939 "guenchi" () (del "8pniyrtk.22"))
b7bf5a4c (290 1790691096430 "guenchi" () (put ((kind . code) (mode . datum) (lang . chez) (body define (shell title desc here body) (join (list "<!doctype html>" (html (quasiquote (html (@ (lang "en")) (head (meta (@ (charset "utf-8"))) (meta (@ (name "viewport") (content "width=device-width, initial-scale=1"))) (title (unquote title)) (meta (@ (name "description") (content (unquote desc)))) (link (@ (rel "icon") (href "favicon.svg?v=2") (type "image/svg+xml"))) (style (raw (unquote (copy "Stylesheet"))))) (body (unquote (topnav here)) (unquote-splicing body) (unquote (foot))))))))) (doc . "") (parent . "8pniyrtk.2") (ord . 70))))
17ae1ab6 (291 1790692494863 "guenchi" () (del "8pniyrtk.80"))
d6f48600 (292 1790692523545 "guenchi" () (put ((kind . code) (mode . datum) (lang . chez) (body define (page-index) (shell "Theourgia -- a block-graph storage engine for LLM agents" "A knowledge base agents and people write into together: a minimal query surface, one graph across code and prose, backlinks in one query, deterministic context assembly, a shared editor, scratchpads with per-block optimistic commits, and Scheme blocks that run." "Home" (list (quasiquote (header (div (@ (class "wrap")) (div (@ (class "glyph")) (raw "&#952;")) (h1 "Theourgia") (p (@ (class "tag")) (unquote (copy "Tagline"))) (p (@ (class "sub")) (unquote (copy "Hero sub"))) (div (@ (class "cta")) (a (@ (class "btn primary") (href "https://github.com/guenchi/theourgia")) "Get the code") (a (@ (class "btn ghost") (href "why.html")) "Why not markdown") (a (@ (class "btn ghost") (href "manual.html")) "The 32 verbs"))))) (sec "features" "Core features" "A Living Graph Engine for Human-Agent Symbiosis" #f (prose "Core features lead")) (sec "query" "01" "A Minimal Query Surface for Agents" (copy "F1 lead") (code-of "F1 example")) (sec "graph" "02" "One Unified Graph Across Docs and Source Code" (copy "F2 lead") (graph-svg) (quasiquote (div (@ (class "grid2")) (unquote (card "A name is a block")) (unquote (card "Other languages, more modestly")))) (quasiquote (p (@ (style "margin-top:22px")) (a (@ (href "manual.html")) "The store, the block and the log, in full") " ->"))) (sec "refs" "03" "Global Backlinks at Near-Zero Cost" (copy "F3 lead") (code-of "Refs, verbatim") (prose "F3 measurement") (table-of "F3 cost table")) (sec "context" "04" "Deterministic Context Assembly" (copy "F4 lead") (prose "Context two layers") (ulist-of "Context sub-features")) (sec "people" "05" "Human-Agent Symbiosis in the IDE" (copy "F5 lead") (ulist-of "IDE scarce uses")) (sec "concurrency" "06" "Zero-Conflict Concurrent Workspaces & Isolated Execution" (copy "F6 lead") (ulist-of "Concurrency sub-features") (code-of "A refusal, verbatim")) (sec "evaluate" "07" "A Lisp Machine: A Living Knowledge Base" (copy "F7 lead") (ulist-of "Lisp Machine sub-features") (code-of "History evaluation, verbatim") (quasiquote (p (@ (class "lead") (style "margin-top:18px")) "The definition was changed between the two calls. The second asks for the " "earlier cut and gets the behaviour that was there then."))) (sec "measured" "Measured" "Numbers, and where they came from" #f (nums-panel "Numbers") (note-of "How the numbers were taken")) (sec "start" "Start" "A store is a directory" #f (code-of "Quickstart") (quasiquote (p (@ (class "lead") (style "margin-top:22px")) (unquote (copy "Install")))))))) (doc . "") (parent . "8pniyrtk.2") (ord . 71))))
423e9557 (293 1790692764739 "guenchi" () (set "8pniyrtk.4q" src "We built a compact interface for token budgets, and stripped out the rendering markup. Core verbs like outline, search, refs, and batch answer in dense S-expressions, one item per line. An agent can see the token footprint of what it is about to read before reading it—and there is no second, pretty-printed output mode to parse."))
7355ff5b (294 1790692773267 "guenchi" () (set "8pniyrtk.4s" src "The wall between the code repository and the document store is a filesystem accident, not a property of the work itself. Here, blocks hold both Markdown documentation and source code files—everything engineering produces lives in one unified graph. A design section, a full source file, a Scheme macro, a Python function, and an architectural decision record are all equal blocks, each with its own stable ID and each independently addressable. Edges are typed and directed, so you can walk from a requirement to the code that meets it, to the test that checks it, back to the discussion that decided it."))
a676913d (295 1790692780023 "guenchi" () (set "8pniyrtk.4t" src "The graph changes how an agent—or a human—hunts for context, and what that hunt costs. A single refs query answers the whole picture at once: which design mentions this function? which prose block refers to it? log gives you the block's full history, and search lands on the one block that answers—so the agent reads that block, not the whole file around it."))
b663bae1 (296 1790692949123 "guenchi" () (set "8pniyrtk.4u" src "An agent's real bottleneck isn't I/O speed—it's whether the tens of thousands of bytes entering its context window are actually right and complete. Today, agents assemble context by intuition: run a search, read a few blocks, feel like it's enough, and start coding. If they miss a premise or follow a superseded ruling, the mistake only surfaces after the work is done. We turn \"gathering materials\" from an agent's heuristic into a deterministic store verb—and make the store show its work."))
25f01402 (297 1790692954163 "guenchi" () (set "8pniyrtk.4v" src "The store isn't just for the automated half; it is a shared semantic layer where humans and agents work on the same code blocks, prose blocks, edges, and history. For humans, that means an IDE, not a CLI. Because people edit real files projected by the store, the Language Server works natively without losing IntelliSense—while the extension maps every save back to the blocks it touched and adds what only the graph knows:"))
88f0fd0a (298 1790692958561 "guenchi" () (set "8pniyrtk.7t" src "The store keeps knowledge and code — and runs them, too."))
b1630c15 (299 1790692965372 "guenchi" () (set "8pniyrtk.5g" src "Above Every Definition, What Only the Graph Knows:|A semantic lens sits right above each function: three design sections refer to this, two lessons learned, last changed by agent-b under request R, see test W3. Hovering reveals the design summary. While the language server tells you what a symbol is, the graph tells you why it is here, who depends on it, and what to read before changing it.\nA Rename That Names the Docs It Left Behind:|An editor rename writes back as one atomic change. Because block IDs never move, every edge from a design section, lesson, or test survives intact. One query for the old name then lists the prose paragraphs that haven't caught up—flagging stale documentation by name instead of hoping somebody notices.\nAn Agent's Draft, Reviewed with the Whole IDE:|Each writer's scratchpad is its own indexed workspace root. You review an agent's unfinished code change alongside its design, references, and live diagnostics rather than squinting at a flat text diff—and the agent sees the same IDE diagnostics and test results on its draft before committing.\nPrecision Test Runs:|With call hierarchies stored as graph edges, knowing which tests must rerun is a single graph walk from the changed block: only the tests that guard it, and the tests that guard its callers, get executed."))
49975bfc (300 1790692972144 "guenchi" () (set "8pniyrtk.7v" src "In-Memory Datalog Queries (query):|The store's reduced in-memory state is treated as a set of logical facts: blocks, their types, validity, and versions; block fields; parent-child trees; library definitions; verification records; task premises; and typed edges (depends, uses, implements, supersedes, refutes). Over these facts sits a fixed set of Datalog-style rules built right into the core. Evaluation runs purely in memory—no disk writes, no log scanning, and no user code execution. Agents can directly ask for dependency chains, blast radiuses, unresolved rulings, expired verifications, or the single authoritative definition of a name in scope without walking the graph by hand.\nBudget-Bounded Context Compilation (context):|Given a task block (carrying its premises, goals, and deliverables) and a strict token budget, context selects and categorizes the working set: Constraints (Must-Read) include the task's premises and their dependency closure, unresolved rulings in the subtree, and the unique, live, authoritative definition for every symbol the task touches within its scope. Evidence, Counterexamples, Background, and Stale Verifications fill the remaining token budget greedily in a documented order. Explicit Exclusions list every block left out due to budget limits alongside why it missed the cut."))
38e4b769 (301 1790692981690 "guenchi" () (set "8pniyrtk.7x" src "In-Block Sandboxed Evaluation:|When a block holds Scheme code, the system acts as a modern Lisp machine. Both agent-generated and human-typed code evaluate in place against the R6RS libraries and definitions held in the store. Every evaluation runs inside an isolated child process with strict wall-clock, memory, and output quotas, returning standard output cleanly in its own response field.\nEvaluate at Any Point in History:|Because the store's state is a deterministic reduction of the log, you can evaluate code at any historical cut. You're not diffing old source text. You're running the old behavior, as the system stood then, with the historical coordinate returned so the run can always be reproduced."))
4bdaee41 (302 1790692989452 "guenchi" () (set "8pniyrtk.4p" src "To get past these limits, the system stops organizing content by files. Blocks now store both documentation and actual source code files. The underlying store still projects onto standard files when needed, but a file boundary no longer decides what is read, what is written, or what is run. Instead, we rebuilt how engineering knowledge and code are structured, assembled, tested, and computed across seven pieces."))
df3a56cd (303 1790693022275 "guenchi" () (del "8pniyrtk.84"))
